# GORA Locked Design

This design is locked for Prompt 4 and every later prompt. Do not rename, reorder, or drop
items without an explicit instruction from the user. Build only what the current prompt asks for.

## Navigation
- Bottom tabs, exactly 7 and in order: Home, Search, Discover, Create (+), Reels, Chat, Profile.
  Never add an 8th (no Clubs tab). Routes: /home, /search, /discover, /create, /reels, /chat, /profile.
- Create (+) opens the create action sheet (the /create route lists the same actions).
- Responsive, Facebook-style web view (mobile/src/theme/responsive.css): under 768px is the phone layout;
  768px+ centers pages in a 680px column; 1024px+ moves the same 7 tabs, in order, into a top bar
  (DesktopTopNav: avatar + GORA + search pill left, tab icons center, filter + bell right) and hides the
  bottom bar; 1240px+ adds a shortcuts sidebar (left) and friend requests + contacts (right) on Home and Discover.
- Header: profile avatar TOP-LEFT (a secondary shortcut, not the primary Profile entry), GORA branding,
  filter icon + notifications bell TOP-RIGHT (filter sits beside the bell). Every main tab except Reels.
- Avatar tap opens a dropdown: Profile, My Games, My Reels, My Stories, Friends, Badges, Activity, Settings.
- Filter tap opens a Tinder-style dropdown: maximum-distance slider (1, 5, 10, 25, 50, 100 km, Any)
  and a sport dropdown. It applies to Home, Search, and Discover.

## Home (bottom tab)
- Social sports newsfeed: stories, a composer that opens Create Post, then one feed mixing
  POST (photo or text, Like/Comment/Share), GAME (host note + game card with PLAYERS, View Game,
  Request to Join), REEL (preview), and ACTIVITY (game completed/joined, badge unlocked).
- Newest first. No ranking algorithm until a prompt asks for one.

## Create Post
Create (+) -> Create Post (/create/post) -> caption -> photos -> 👤 Tag People -> 📍 Add Location -> sport -> privacy -> publish.
The post appears on Home, Profile, and Search. Images now; video later.
- Tags (PostTag, unique per post+user, never the author, max 20): friends first, never blocked users. Card shows
 "with A, B" (more than 3 names: "and N others"). Only the author adds or removes tags ("⋯" -> Edit tags).
 Tagging never changes who can see a post. Tag notifications come later.
- Location is optional: Post.locationName/latitude/longitude, all three or none, picked explicitly by the author
 (search GORA venues -> select -> Confirm Location; current location / select on map come with the map provider).
 Card shows "📍 Name", which opens the location view.
- Privacy selector: 🌎 Public, 👥 Friends, ⚙️ Custom, 🔒 Only Me (PostVisibility PUBLIC/FRIENDS/CUSTOM/ONLY_ME).
 Custom = only the chosen people (PostCustomViewer) plus the author; never "all friends"; nobody preselected.
- Cards show a privacy indicator only, never the viewer list. The author edits privacy from "⋯"; it applies at once.
- Author "⋯" menu, in order: Edit post, Edit privacy, Tag people / Edit tags, Delete post (destructive), Cancel.
 Edit post (EditPostModal, PATCH /posts/:id) changes caption (never empty), sport, and location only, sets editedAt,
 and the card shows "· Edited". Delete post confirms "Delete post?" then DELETE /posts/:id = soft delete (Post.deletedAt;
 row, likes, comments, tags kept; hidden from everyone incl. the author; later reads 404). Never hard-delete posts.
- Posts are stored in PostgreSQL when signed in: stores/posts.ts loads GET /posts (Home feed, newest first) plus the
 account's GET /users/:username/posts, publishes with POST /posts (sport name -> sportId). Real posts (fromServer) come
 first and are never re-filtered on the client; demo posts stay beside them, changed locally only. No photo upload yet
 (photo picker hidden while signed in); Tag People / Custom list only real accounts (none until the Friends system).

## Post privacy (backend-enforced)
- server/src/posts/post-visibility.ts visiblePostsWhere(viewerId) is the only visibility rule; every post read uses it.
 Author sees all; others: PUBLIC; FRIENDS only if ACCEPTED friends; CUSTOM only if listed; ONLY_ME never.
 A block in either direction, an inactive author, or a private club (non-member) hides posts.
- Hidden and missing posts both answer 404. Custom viewers are returned only to the author. The client mirror
 (mobile/src/utils/post-privacy.ts) is for mock data only; never rely on the frontend for privacy.

## Other users' profiles
- /profile/:username (not a tab; /users/:username redirects there; your own username redirects to /profile).
 Reached from post authors, player rows, Discover players, request names, and the chat header.
- Read-only, from GET /profiles/:username: no Edit Profile, no Settings, never dateOfBirth or email. Counts cover
 only what the viewer may see. Unknown, inactive, and BLOCKED_BY_THEM users answer 404.
- Reserved usernames (server/src/users/reserved-usernames.ts, mirrored in mobile/src/utils/auth.ts) cannot be
 registered because they clash with /profile/* routes.
- Buttons come from the relationship state (server/src/social/relationship.ts, mobile/src/utils/relationship.ts):
 NO_RELATIONSHIP [Add Friend][Message], REQUEST_SENT [Request Sent][Message], REQUEST_RECEIVED [Accept][Delete],
 FRIENDS [Friends][Message], BLOCKED [Unblock]. BLOCKED_BY_THEM answers 404. No self friend requests.
- Message: friends -> direct conversation; non-friends -> the same chat screen (/chat/request/:userId) whose first
 message is the one message request per pair (then "Waiting for X to accept…"); blocked -> none. Never a popup.
- The full Friends system (add/accept/reject/block endpoints, followers lists) and profile privacy come later.

## Profile (bottom tab)
- Data comes from GET /profiles/me (server/src/profiles/) through the profile Pinia store; never fabricate counts.
- Header: cover photo (User.coverImageUrl), avatar with story ring, display name (formatDisplayName helper),
  @username, city with a location icon, bio (max 160), and an [Edit Profile] button (/profile/edit).
- Then 3 tappable stats (Friends, Followers, Following), the section links, MY SPORTS [+ Add Sport],
  MY CLUBS (every club you are an ACTIVE member of as "[Club] 24/50 Members · Role", See all clubs; no Create Club
  here), HIGHLIGHTS (3 newest, See all -> My Reels), and MY FEED with a "Share a game moment…" composer (opens
  Create Post) above ONLY the signed-in account's own posts (never anyone else's). New posts are authored by the
  signed-in account (postsStore.me), not the demo user.
- Sections, in order: My Games, My Reels, My Stories, Friends, Followers, Following, Badges, Activity, My Clubs,
  Settings. Shown as plain text links: the first 4 in a row, the rest under "More ▾" (each with its summary).
  The avatar dropdown keeps its 8 items.
- Edit Profile (/profile/edit): photo URL, first/last name, bio, city, date of birth, cover URL; Save and Cancel.
  Username and email cannot be changed there. Images are URLs; uploads are a stub (services/upload.service.ts).
- MY SPORTS: UserSport with skill level BEGINNER/INTERMEDIATE/ADVANCED/PROFESSIONAL and optional position
  (max 40; suggestions for Basketball, Volleyball, Football). One entry per sport; add, edit, remove.
  Add: Sport tiles (icon, name, selected check) -> Skill Level -> optional Position -> [Save Sport]. Edit changes level and
  position only. Remove asks "Remove Volleyball from your sports?" [Cancel] [Remove] and deletes only the UserSport row.
- Friends has two parts: Friends and Requests (Received with Accept/Decline, Sent with Cancel).

## Sports (Prompt 7)
- One central Sport table (id, unique name, description, iconUrl, isActive) used by UserSport, Game (required),
 and the optional Post/Reel/Club sportId and ClubSport. Never duplicate Sport or UserSport. The 10 seeded sports:
 Basketball, Volleyball, Football, Tennis, Badminton, Running, Table Tennis, Swimming, Cycling, Other (seed upserts by
 name and never touches isActive). Only active sports are listed or addable; retired ones stay for history.
- Users only read sports: GET /sports (active, {id,name,description,iconUrl,isActive}), GET /sports/:id. No create,
 edit, activate, or delete route (future admin module).
- Own sports: GET|POST /users/me/sports, PATCH|DELETE /users/me/sports/:sportId (server/src/sports/user-sports.*,
 UserSportsService, exported). Owner from the JWT only; userId in a body is 400. Unknown/retired sport 404,
 duplicate 409, bad UUID 400 (body) or 404 (path). /profiles/me/sports is an alias using the same service.
- Client: stores/sports.ts (fetchSports, fetchMySports, addSport, updateSport, removeSport; cached, one request at a
 time) via services/sports-api.service.ts; it syncs profile.currentProfile.sports. components/sports/SportIcon.vue
 shows iconUrl, else the built-in icon for the name; the icon is never the identity (the id is).
- Search tiles, the sport page, and Discover Trending Sports still use the demo catalog stats (services/mock).

## Chat (bottom tab)
- Three tabs, in order: [Friends] (conversations with accepted friends), [Clubs] (official club chats:
  club image, name, last message, time, unread), [Requests] (Message Requests from non-friends, then Sent).
- Message Request: Accept -> conversation becomes active; Delete -> rejected/removed.
  One request per pair of users, so requests cannot be spammed. Block/Report come later.
- Conversation screen at /chat/:conversationId. Game group chats (type GAME) are supported by the
  schema but not built yet.
- Group chats belong ONLY to clubs. Never add "Create Group" / "New Group", a group-creation endpoint,
  DIRECT -> group conversion, or adding arbitrary users. DIRECT is 2 people (trigger-enforced).
- ConversationType DIRECT | GAME | CLUB (Conversation_context_check). Exactly one CLUB chat per club
  (Conversation.clubId @unique), created by the Club_create_chat trigger in the club's transaction.
- Club chat access is derived from ClubMember only: ACTIVE (any role) in an active club. PENDING, REMOVED,
  BANNED, non-members: no access. Never copy members into the conversation; participant rows are read state.
- Endpoints: GET /chat/clubs, GET /clubs/:clubId/chat, GET|POST /clubs/:clubId/chat/messages
  (server/src/clubs/club-chat.*). Each checks user, club exists (404), active (403), ACTIVE membership (403),
  CLUB chat of that club. Sender comes from the JWT; extra body fields are 400. Triggers also guard senders.
- Club chat screen /chat/clubs/:clubId: club image, name, "Members: N", "Official Club Chat" banner,
  sender names, "Type a message..." + Send; visually distinct from DMs. Club page [Chat] button is
  disabled unless ACTIVE. Inactive club: history kept, no new messages. Chat badge includes club unread.
- Permissions: OWNER/ADMIN manage, MODERATOR+ moderate, MEMBER reads and sends. Pins, announcements,
  media, polls, mentions, deletion, moderation actions, and push notifications come later.

## Search (Spotify-style browse, for sports)
- Search across: Players, Sports, Games, Locations, Posts, Reels, Clubs.
- Browse with sports category tiles.
- Distance filters: 1 km, 5 km, 10 km, 25 km, 50 km, 100 km, Any.
- No distance or sport chips on the Search page; those live in the header filter.
- Tapping a sport opens its full section at /search/:sport (games, players, clubs, reels, locations, posts)
 with a "Search in <Sport>" box that filters every section, date chips for games ([All] default = every upcoming
 game; Today, Tomorrow, This Week are optional; Custom later), and a [Map] [List] toggle. Posts are every visible
 post of that sport, newest first, as full post cards; the date chips never hide posts.
- Game discovery map (Prompt 11, docs/features/sport-map-discovery.md): markers are real GORA games from
 GET /games/discover only (never real-world courts, never demo data), sport emoji markers (getSportMarker; the Sport id
 is the identity), statuses OPEN/FULL/ACTIVE (never CANCELLED; COMPLETED only on request), games closer than 100 m share
 one marker. Marker preview = DiscoveredGameCard: sport, "Today • 6:00 PM", place, "1.2 km away", "Players: 8/12",
 "Hosted by @user", [View Game] [Request to Join] (existing join request flow). Counts and distance come from the server.
 Map provider abstraction (services/map-provider.ts): VITE_MAP_PROVIDER / VITE_MAP_API_KEY from env only, never
 hardcoded; unset, keyless, or not-yet-connected providers fall back to the built-in PlaceholderMapCanvas (no key,
 no network). No map packages or external APIs until a prompt adds a provider adapter (MapCanvasProps contract).
- Device location (services/location.service.ts): asked only from "Use my location" (or reused if already granted),
 a denial is remembered, never re-prompted. Rounded (~110 m), memory only, sent only as the discovery search center;
 never stored (no User column, no UserLocation table, no local storage), never public. Denied/unavailable shows
 "Location access is unavailable. You can still browse GORA games by sport and date." and browsing still works.
- Location view /map/:lat/:lng?name=&game= (not a tab), opened by tapping 📍 on a post, game card, or Game Details
 (📍 name + [View on Map], only when the game has coordinates): GameDiscoveryMap centered on the place, real GORA games
 within 2 km (discovery.discoverAround). From a game, that game is "Selected game" and always shown.
- Post location (social context) and Game location (required venue + sportId, gameDate, startTime, endTime, status)
 stay separate; only games become markers. Never expose home locations; no GPS or background tracking.

## Create (+) actions
Create Post, Create Game, Upload Reel, Add Story, Go Live.

## Games (Prompt 8)
- Module server/src/games/ (GamesController -> GamesService -> Prisma). POST /games, GET /games
 (?sportId&status&gameDate=upcoming|today|YYYY-MM-DD&limit&offset; soonest first; default OPEN/FULL/ACTIVE, today on),
 GET /games/mine (hosted), GET /games/playing (ACTIVE seat), GET /games/:id, PATCH /games/:id (host only, OPEN/FULL only), PATCH /games/:id/cancel
 (host only, sets CANCELLED, never deletes). Never a DELETE route.
- GET /games/discover (declared before :gameId; GameDiscoveryService, separate from CRUD, read-only):
 ?sportId (UUID; unknown/retired 404) &date (today|tomorrow|this-week|YYYY-MM-DD, default upcoming, GAME_TIMEZONE clock)
 &latitude&longitude (both or neither, -90..90 / -180..180, blanks and text 400, never 0) &distanceKm (0.1-100, needs a
 center; omitted = Any) &status (OPEN|FULL|ACTIVE|COMPLETED; default OPEN/FULL/ACTIVE; CANCELLED 400) &limit (1-100, 50).
 visibleGamesWhere always applies. Distance = Haversine in server/src/games/geo-distance.ts (bounding-box prefilter;
 PostGIS later), nearest first with a center, else soonest first. Games without coordinates never appear in radius
 results (listed with distanceKm null otherwise). Response {games[DiscoveredGameView], dateFrom, dateTo, distanceKm};
 host = id, username, firstName, lastName, displayName, profileImageUrl only; currentPlayers = ACTIVE GameParticipant rows.
- CreateGameDto: sportId, clubId?, title (3-80), description? (500), requiredPlayers (1-100), gameDate, startTime,
 endTime, locationName (2-120), latitude?/longitude? (both or neither). hostId from the JWT only; hostId, status,
 counts, timestamps in a body are 400. New games are OPEN; status is never set by the client.
- gameDate "YYYY-MM-DD" and "HH:mm" times are the venue's wall clock (timestamp without time zone), never shifted.
 Today is decided in GAME_TIMEZONE (default Asia/Manila). Date today..+365 days; end > start; today cannot start in the past.
- Sport must be active (else 404). Club: exists (404), active (403), host ACTIVE member (HOST_CLUB_GAMES, 403).
- visibleGamesWhere (server/src/games/game-visibility.ts) is the only game visibility rule: host, or active host with
 no block and a null / public / member club. Hidden and missing games both answer 404.
- Client: stores/games.ts (createGame, fetchGame, fetchGames, fetchMyGames, updateGame, cancelGame; cache by id) via
 services/games-api.service.ts; utils/game-form.ts mirrors the rules. /create/game (Create Game), /games/:gameId/edit,
 Game Details for UUID ids (ServerGameDetails), My Games = Hosting (GET /games/mine) + Playing (GET /games/playing,
 fetchPlayingGames) + Past & cancelled. GameView.isPlayer = viewer has an ACTIVE seat. The demo `games` list
 still feeds Home, Search, Discover, and the sport page.

## Join requests (Prompt 9)
- Existing JoinRequest model (unique per game+user, no migration). server/src/games/join-requests.* (JoinRequestsController ->
 JoinRequestsService -> Prisma). POST /games/:gameId/join-requests {message? max 300}, GET .../me ({joinRequest|null}),
 PATCH .../me/cancel, GET .../join-requests (host only), PATCH .../:requestId/accept, PATCH .../:requestId/reject (host only).
- Requester/host from the JWT only; any other body field is 400. Only PENDING moves: -> ACCEPTED/REJECTED (host, respondedAt)
 or CANCELLED (requester). Conditional updateMany; loser 409. Never delete rows.
- Create: visible game (else 404), not the host (403), OPEN and not started (409; FULL = "This game is already full."),
 not an ACTIVE player, no PENDING/REJECTED row (409). A CANCELLED row, or an ACCEPTED row whose player left or was
 removed, is reused (back to PENDING); declined is final for that game.
- Accept: one transaction locking the Game row; request PENDING, game OPEN and not started, requester active and
 unblocked, ACTIVE players < requiredPlayers (409); then request -> ACCEPTED and GameParticipant upserted to ACTIVE
 (reusing the row). The trigger sets FULL at capacity. Old pending requests on a FULL game stay PENDING, never auto-accepted.
- Host list: requester id, username, first/last name, displayName, profileImageUrl only. GameView.pendingRequestCount
 (host only, else null).
- Client: stores/join-requests.ts (createJoinRequest, fetchMyJoinRequest, cancelJoinRequest, fetchGameJoinRequests,
 acceptJoinRequest, rejectJoinRequest; one action at a time) via services/join-requests-api.service.ts;
 utils/join-requests.ts decides the button. ServerGameDetails: [Request to Join] -> JoinRequestModal (message,
 [Cancel] [Send Request]); PENDING: disabled [Request Pending] + [Cancel Request]; ACTIVE player: [Leave Game];
 REJECTED: "Request declined". Host: HostJoinRequests ("Pending Requests: N", [Accept] [Reject], answered history).

## Players (Prompt 10)
- Existing GameParticipant (unique per game+user, status ACTIVE/LEFT/COMPLETED/REMOVED), no migration.
 server/src/games/game-players.* (GamePlayersController -> GamePlayersService -> Prisma); helpers in game-roster.ts
 (lockGame, countSeatedPlayers, withCapacityGuard, GAME_FULL_MESSAGE) and game-capacity.ts.
- GET /games/:gameId/players {gameId, requiredPlayers, currentPlayers, availableSlots, status, players[id, username,
 firstName, lastName, displayName, profileImageUrl, joinedAt]} (ACTIVE only, join order; visible game else 404).
 GET .../players/me {gameId, status ACTIVE|LEFT|COMPLETED|REMOVED|NOT_A_PLAYER, joinedAt, completedAt}.
 PATCH .../players/me/leave (ACTIVE -> LEFT). PATCH .../players/:userId/remove (host only 403; not self 400; ACTIVE -> REMOVED).
 No body is read. Missing seat 404, non-ACTIVE seat or ACTIVE/COMPLETED game 409.
- Count = ACTIVE rows only, everywhere (GameView.currentPlayers and the roster). Never delete participant rows; rejoin
 reactivates the same row, so never two ACTIVE seats. Leave/remove lock the Game row; the trigger reopens FULL -> OPEN.
 CANCELLED/ACTIVE/COMPLETED are never changed by roster moves; ACTIVE/COMPLETED lifecycle is not automated.
- Capacity: service count under the row lock + GameParticipant_capacity_guard trigger (mapped to 409
 "This game is already full."). Concurrent accepts for the last seat: one 200, one 409, never 13/12.
- Client: stores/game-players.ts (fetchPlayers, fetchMyParticipation, leaveGame, removePlayer, refreshGameCount; one
 action at a time) via services/game-players-api.service.ts; the join requests store refreshes the count after
 accept/reject. ServerGameDetails "Player Roster": players (link /profile/:username, "You"), then Open slots from
 buildRosterSlots (never fake users). Host: [Manage Players] -> [Remove Player] per row (confirm). Player: [Leave Game] (confirm).
 Left/removed users see why and may request again.

## Stories
- 24-hour expiry: `expiresAt = createdAt + 24h`; rings; "Your Story" first, then others.
- Expired stories are hidden, never deleted (kept for a future archive/history).
- Music is optional: Story.musicTrackId/musicTitle/musicArtist/musicStartTime/musicDuration (seconds).
  MusicTrack references a licensed provider. Never store or download copyrighted audio.
  Planned flow: Photo/Video -> Add Music -> search -> track -> segment -> preview -> post.
- Stored in PostgreSQL (server/src/stories/). Add Story (/create/story, from Create (+) and the Your Story add button):
 Photo/Video link (http(s); uploads later), caption (max 500), privacy. Story.visibility uses PostVisibility
 (PUBLIC/FRIENDS/CUSTOM/ONLY_ME, custom viewers in StoryCustomViewer); visibleStoriesWhere is the only rule.
- The author's "⋯" menu (story viewer, My Stories): Edit caption, Edit privacy, Delete (confirm). Delete is soft
 (Story.deletedAt): hidden for everyone, including the author and My Stories; the row is kept.

## Reels
- Vertical full-screen video feed with Like, Comment, Share, Follow, and player/sport context.
- TikTok-style: no app header on Reels. The video fills the screen; overlaid on top are the text tabs
  centered and a LIVE button TOP-RIGHT (opens live viewing; a later-phase notice until Live exists).
  The 7 bottom tabs stay visible.
- Tabs: Following | For You (For You is the default). Following = reels from accounts the viewer follows.
- For You recommendations are not implemented; the database (ReelView, likes, comments, shares,
  follows, sport) only supports them. The client shows the order it receives.
- Reels are Profile HIGHLIGHTS / My Reels, stored in PostgreSQL (server/src/reels/). Upload Reel (/create/reel):
 video link (uploads later), optional thumbnail link, caption (max 2200), optional sport, privacy.
 ReelVisibility PUBLIC/FRIENDS/CUSTOM/ONLY_ME (custom viewers in ReelCustomViewer); visibleReelsWhere is the only rule.
- The author's "⋯" menu (Highlights, My Reels, Reels tab): Edit reel (caption, sport), Edit privacy, Delete (confirm,
 soft via Reel.deletedAt). Highlights and My Reels show only the signed-in account's reels; the Reels tab lists
 real reels first, then the demo reels.

## Follows
- UserFollow (followerId, followingId, createdAt): one-way, unique per pair, no self-follow.
- Follow and Friendship are separate and never combined. Following needs no approval;
 friendship needs a request and Accept and drives Friends and Chat.
- Friendship.blockedById records who blocked whom (set exactly when status is BLOCKED).

## Discover
Feed filters [All] [Friends] [Clubs], All first.
- All: Popular Players, Trending Sports, Popular Games, Trending Reels, Nearby GORA Games, Featured Athletes,
 Popular Clubs, Public Posts.
- Nearby GORA Games (components/discover/NearbyGamesSection.vue, stores/discovery.ts): [Sport] (All Sports + active
 sports) and [Distance] (1, 5, 10, 25, 50, 100 km, Any) ARE the header filter (filters store, no duplicate state);
 Date chips All, Today, Tomorrow, This Week, Custom Date; [Map] [List] show the same results. Distance applies only
 with a device location (else "Distance needs your location"). Empty: "No GORA games found nearby." / "Try increasing
 the distance or selecting another date." Search -> sport page Map view hands off to /discover?sport=&date=&view=map.
- Friends: accepted friends plus followed users. Clubs: clubs the user belongs to (ACTIVE) or follows.
- No recommendation algorithm yet; placeholder ordering only. Later: Recommended Games.
Search = user searches; Discover = GORA recommends.

## Clubs
- Club (owner, unique slug, sport, location, isPublic, isActive), ClubMember (role OWNER/ADMIN/MODERATOR/MEMBER,
  status PENDING/ACTIVE/REMOVED/BANNED, unique per club+user), ClubFollow (one-way, unique per club+user).
- The owner's OWNER/ACTIVE membership is trigger-managed; one OWNER per club. Never insert it from app code.
- Post/Game/Reel.clubId are optional and require an ACTIVE member of an active club. The club never replaces
  the game host ("Hosted by Louis" + club label).
- Membership, ClubFollow, Friendship, and UserFollow are separate and never combined.
- Access: Profile -> My Clubs (/profile/clubs), Settings -> Create Club (/profile/clubs/new; the only Create Club
  entry), Search -> Clubs, sport page,
  Discover -> Clubs, club labels on games/posts/reels. Club page at /clubs/:clubId: "24 / 50 Members", "26 slots
  available" (or FULL), [Join Club] / [Request to Join] / [Accept Invite] / [Club Full] / [Invite Only], [Chat]
  (ACTIVE only), [Manage Club] (owner/admin), Follow, tabs [Posts] [Games] [Reels] [Members]. Private clubs hide
  content, rules, schedule, and links from non-members; contact email shows to ACTIVE members only.
- Create Club (server/src/clubs/clubs.*, POST /clubs): name, @username (= slug, unique, normalized), photo/cover URLs,
  short description (max 160), about; primary sport + up to 5 additional (ClubSport); country, city, barangay,
  home court, location name, optional typed coordinates; maxMembers* (presets 10-1000 or custom, 1..CLUB_MAX_MEMBERS_LIMIT,
  default 1000); membershipType OPEN / APPROVAL_REQUIRED / INVITE_ONLY; Public / Private; rules (ClubRule, max 20);
  tags (ClubTag, normalized, max 10); informational schedule (never creates games); contact email + website/Facebook/
  Instagram/TikTok. One transaction: club + OWNER/ACTIVE owner (trigger) + one CLUB chat (trigger), else rollback.
  Success: "CLUB CREATED!", "You are the Owner.", "Members: 1 / N", [Go to Club] [Open Club Chat].
- Capacity: currentMembers / availableSlots / isFull are counted from ACTIVE ClubMember rows only, never stored.
  PENDING and invites use no slot. Join and approve lock the Club row and recount ("Club is currently full.", 409);
  ClubMember_capacity_guard enforces it in the DB, so 49/50 never becomes 51/50. maxMembers cannot drop below the
  ACTIVE count (Club_max_members_guard); members are never auto-removed. Separate from Game.requiredPlayers.
- Join rules are server-side: OPEN joins instantly, APPROVAL_REQUIRED makes PENDING, INVITE_ONLY needs a pending
  ClubInvite (an invite skips approval). Only the owner edits settings (PATCH /clubs/:clubId); OWNER/ADMIN handle
  requests, invites, and removals at /clubs/:clubId/manage. Demo (mock) clubs cannot be managed.
- Demo clubs: a signed-in account starts with NO demo membership/follow/invite/manage rights (asNonMember);
  only clubs it joins or creates are "its" clubs. The demo user's memberships are never shown as the account's.
  Actions in the app use session.me (the signed-in account), never the demo user, when someone is signed in.
- Permissions (server/src/clubs/club-permissions.ts): OWNER manages club/admins/members and disables;
  ADMIN posts, games, members, content; MODERATOR content, reports, comments; MEMBER views, participates, hosts club games, posts.
- Full moderation (removal, bans, report review UI) comes later.

## Authentication (Prompt 5)
- Server: auth/ (register, login, GET /auth/me, JwtStrategy, JwtAuthGuard, @CurrentUser) and users/ (UsersService).
 Controller -> AuthService -> UsersService -> PrismaService. Argon2id hashing. Always use the safe selects in
 users/user.types.ts; never return passwordHash, never log passwords or tokens.
- JWT payload is only { sub, username, role }; JWT_SECRET (min 32 chars) and JWT_EXPIRES_IN (default 7d) come from env.
 JwtStrategy reloads the user and rejects inactive accounts. Login failures return "Invalid credentials.".
- Client: stores/auth.ts, services/api-client.ts, services/auth.service.ts, services/token-storage.ts.
 /login and /register are guestOnly; the tab layout (every tab and sub-page) is requiresAuth. Log Out lives in Settings
 (not in the avatar dropdown, which keeps its 8 items) and is client-side only.
- Not built: social login, 2FA, password reset, email verification, admin dashboard, token revocation.

## Database
- Prisma schema in server/prisma/schema.prisma holds all 42 GORA models (the original 26 plus MusicTrack,
 UserFollow, PostShare, ReelView, ReelShare, Club, ClubMember, ClubFollow, PostCustomViewer, PostTag, ClubSport, ClubTag,
 ClubRule, ClubInvite, StoryCustomViewer, ReelCustomViewer). Never reset the database or
  delete migrations; add new migrations only. 22 migrations so far; the latest is 20260930233100_story_reel_privacy_and_delete.
  Triggers must write timestamps as timezone('UTC', now()), never CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (the DB is not UTC).
- Media (videos, images, live streams) live in external storage; PostgreSQL stores URLs and metadata.

## Activity stats
Games Joined, Games Completed, Games Hosted, Highlights Uploaded, Stories Posted, Friends,
Sports Participated.

## Badges
First Game, Getting Started, Active Player, Dedicated Player, Veteran, Game Host, Organizer,
Team Player, Highlight Creator, Highlight Maker, Social Player, Community Player, Storyteller.

## Game capacity and roster
- Display PLAYERS as ACTIVE GameParticipant rows / Game.requiredPlayers (the DB guards still count COMPLETED too,
  which only matters for finished games). Never store a denormalized player count. Never show more players than
  requiredPlayers (no 13/12).
- The host is not a player just because they created the game. They count only if they join as a participant.
- OPEN while ACTIVE players < requiredPlayers; FULL at capacity. The database rejects over-capacity inserts.
- Game cards (Home, Search, Discover, sport page, Profile / My Games, GamePreviewCard) and Game Details show this count.
  Game Details also lists one slot per required player: accepted players, then Open slots.

## Game flow (backend-owned)
Join Game -> Join Request -> Host Accepts -> Participant -> Game Happens -> Game Completed
-> Activity Updated -> Achievement Checked -> Badge Unlocked -> Notification (top-right bell).

- Only accepted participants of a completed game get activity credit.
- Activity updates, achievement checks, and badge unlocks run on the server; Vue only displays results.
